    "title": "MLB News: Blue Jays Sign Dylan Cease, Angels Seek To Part Ways With Anthony Rendon, Nolan Arenado Update & More - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Cresswell McCoy ,\n1 hours ago\nDylan Cease and Nolan Arenado (Photo By Imagn Images) MLB fans witnessed a flurry of signings over the last couple of days . The New York Mets and Texas Rangers pulled off a trade, and several rumors are swirling around free agents. With the offseason kicking off to a strong start, many teams are already reshaping their roster. One team that is eyeing another run to the World Series again is the Toronto Blue Jays.\nToronto Blue Jays Acquire MLB Free Agent Dylan Cease Dylan Cease (Image Credits: Imagn) The Blue Jays have a solid starting rotation with young players like Trey Yesavage creating history. The franchise almost won the World Series, and they are not ready to give up anytime soon.\nOn Wednesday, Toronto signed former Padres ace and MLB free agent Dylan Cease to a seven-year $210 million deal. Cease will join Kevin Gausman, Shane Bieber, Yesavage, and the other pitching crew. Despite his rough 2025 stint with the Padres, the Blue Jays have taken a chance on Cease.\nLos Angeles Angels Seek To Part Ways With Anthony Rendon Anthony Rendon (Image Credits: Imagn) The last few years for Anthony Rendon have been a disaster. Rendon failed to be consistent in his MLB career with the Angels. He’s missed out on multiple seasons due to injuries, and the Angels want to part ways with the slugger.\nThe team is currently in talks with Rendon, hoping to buy out the final year of his MLB contract. Rumors are that Anthony Rendon might retire from the big leagues.\nMLB Rumors Take A Wild Turn With Nolan Arenado Nolan Arenado (Image Credits: Imagn) Nolan Arenado has been on the trade block for more than a year now. The St. Louis Cardinals are ready to part ways with the slugger. Despite multiple teams being in the mix , Arenado is waiting to find a home.\nRecent MLB rumors have taken a wild turn with the slugger, as the Pirates and Angels have emerged as favorites for the All-Star veteran. Arenado to the Angels makes sense right now, especially since they are looking to part ways with Anthony Rendon.\nThe post originally published on .\n1",
